      "year": 2025,
      "abstract": "abstract:This paper aims to fill a gap in the literature by investigating Fichte\u2019s application of the genetic method to Kant\u2019s transcendental philosophy. I claim that Fichte\u2019s main source for developing this method is Ernst Platner\u2019s conception of logic as a pragmatic history of the human faculty of cognition. To support this claim, I argue (1) that Platner himself reworked Kant\u2019s account of the faculties by using this method, (2) that Fichte engaged extensively with Platner\u2019s approach to Kant, and (3) that he employed a nonpsychological version of Platner\u2019s method to recast Kant\u2019s transcendental logic in the Foundation of the Entire Doctrine of Science. In my view, Fichte\u2019s development of the genetic method within a transcendental framework is one of his most influential contributions to the further development of German Idealism.",
